{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI GREEN ARRIVING ON ps3 — the stacking-order fix is confirmed.\n 2503 parity        LLM +1  Verified +1\n 2504 mirrors       LLM +1  Verified +1\n 2505 atomic        LLM +1  Verified +1\n 2506 guard         LLM +1  Verified +1\n 2507 measurement   LLM +1  Verified pending\n 2510 ratchet       LLM +1  Verified pending\nAll six now carry LLM-Review +1. 2503 passing is the direct proof: it is the commit that carried the\noriginal synthetic-mini-repo failure AND the one I stripped the up-stack markers from.\nDiagnosed the queue rather than waiting blindly — six 'Gerrit Verified Gate' runs were dispatched\ntogether at the push and are draining two-at-a-time behind runner capacity, so the pending votes are\nqueueing, not stuck.\n\nSTARTED CLOSING the four leaves whose change is already green, rather than waiting for the last two:\n8ce5, f9b9, b0ac, 15f2. Sequential, because concurrent closes contend on the store and each runs the\ncompletion verifier. The script reports a refusal rather than working around it — no force."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788336104121354001,"uuid":"65a8c66e-f0eb-48de-a725-a2e41f1c1cec"}